course: dictionary
lesson: 12386
title: Culpable: who is to blame?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Culpable is a formal word. It means deserving blame for something wrong or bad. If you are culpable, the blame belongs to you. «The driver was culpable for the accident.» The words accident and for tell you this is about harm and blame.
explain: Look at the words around it and ask what would fit. Blame, responsible and at fault all fit here. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The driver deserved blame for the accident" makes sense, so culpable must mean deserving blame.
explain: Judges and courts decide how culpable someone is. A person who did not mean any harm may be less culpable than someone who did it on purpose. «The judge said the boy was less culpable, because he had not meant to hurt anyone.»
explain: Culpable is often followed by for, as in culpable for something. Its opposite is blameless: someone who did nothing wrong. When you meet an unknown formal word, read the sentence again, look for the clues, then check a dictionary if you still are not sure.
fact: Culpable means deserving blame for something wrong or bad.
fact: Culpable is a formal word, often used in law, ethics and history.
fact: «He was culpable for the accident» means the blame for the accident was his.
fact: A person who did not mean harm may be less culpable than someone who did it on purpose.
fact: In Scotland, «culpable homicide» means killing someone without meaning to murder them.
exercise: «The driver was culpable for the crash because he was texting.» What does culpable mean? | Happy and relaxed | Very tired | *Deserving blame for something wrong | Feeling cold
exercise: «The judge decided the thief was culpable for the robbery.» Which word is a clue that this is about wrongdoing? | happy | dinner | *robbery | sunny
exercise: Mia says culpable means very clever. What does it really mean? | It means cheerful and full of fun | It means very tall | *It means deserving blame for something wrong, not being clever | It means being quiet in a library
test: «Nobody could say who was culpable for the broken window.» What does culpable mean here? | Very tall | Hungry | *Deserving blame | Shiny and new
test: «The boy did not mean to harm anyone, so he was less culpable than the man who caused the fire on purpose.» Which person was more culpable? | Both were exactly the same | The boy who did not mean harm | *The man who caused the fire on purpose | Neither was near the fire
exam: «The captain was held culpable for the ship's loss, so he had to explain himself to the court.» What does held culpable mean? | *Judged to deserve blame | Lost at sea | Asked to sing a song | Given a medal for bravery
